---
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>About Me | Portfolio</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      background-color: #ffffff;
      color: #1a1a1a;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .about-container {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 4rem 2rem;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; margin: 0; }
    .bio-content { font-size: 1.2rem; color: #222; }
    .bio-content p { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <Navigation />

  <main id="main-content" class="about-container">
    <header>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Kristen.</h1>
    </header>
    
    <article class="bio-content">
      <p>I’m a graphic designer who likes making things for the web.</p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->
  <section-class="intro-section">
    <h2>Designer, problem-solver, and professional perfectionist.</h2>
    <p>I’m a graphic designer with a particular interest in **web design, UX/UI, and digital accessibility**. I love taking something complicated and figuring out how to make it feel simple, intuitive, and maybe even a little fun.</p>
    <p>My approach to design is rooted in curiosity. I want to understand the *why* behind a project before jumping into the *how*. Who is using it? What do they need? What could make their experience easier?</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Accessibility -->
  <section-class="accessibility-section">
    <h2>Design should have no unnecessary barriers.</h2>
    <p>My interest in accessibility comes from believing that the web should be designed with **real people and real differences** in mind.</p>
    <p>Different abilities, devices, environments, and ways of interacting with technology all change how someone experiences a website. I want accessibility to be part of the design process, not a checklist at the end of a project.</p>
    <p>For me, accessible design is simply **good design with more people included.**</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: Personality / Designer Philosophy -->
  <section-class="personality-section">
    <h2>A little more about me</h2>
    <p>I’m happiest when I’m creating, experimenting, or learning something I didn’t know yesterday.</p>
    <p>I’m the kind of designer who will spend way too long adjusting a tiny detail because *I know it could be better*. I love clean layouts, thoughtful typography, interactive websites, and finding those little moments that make a digital experience feel special.</p>
    <p>Outside of design, you’ll probably find me at the gym, spending time with friends, or taking Pokémon Go a little too seriously.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Skills -->
  <section-class="skills-section">
    <h2>I’m pretty good at these</h2>
    <h3>Design</h3>
    <p>Graphic Design <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Branding <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Art Direction <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Typography <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Layout <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Visual Systems</p>
    <h3>Digital</h3>
    <p>Web Design <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Accessibility <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> UX/UI <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Interaction Design <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Responsive Design</p>
    <h3>Tools</h3>
    <p>Adobe Creative Cloud <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Framer <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> HTML <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> CSS <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> JavaScript <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Astro <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Figma </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5: About Closing -->
  <section-class="about-closing-section">
    <h2>Still curious?</h2>
    <p>Curiosity doesn’t kill the cat here.</p>
    <a href="/portfolio/work/" class="cta-link">Explore My Work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>

</body>
</html>
